SOMA-JAX is a derivative work: it reimplements SOMA-X's pipeline (identity
blend, skeletal abstraction, mesh topology abstraction, pose abstraction,
forward FK/LBS and pose inversion) in JAX/equinox in place of the upstream
PyTorch + NVIDIA Warp backend. Rig data, algorithms and API shape derive from
SOMA-X. Upstream SOMA-X is vendored unmodified at `third_party/SOMA-X` as a git
submodule and retains its own LICENSE.

Summary of changes relative to SOMA-X, as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):
see `docs/FAITHFULNESS.md`, which records module by module what is a faithful
port, what is implemented with a different but verified-equivalent structure,
what is an explicitly-flagged SOMA-JAX-only alternative, and what is not ported.

